    "n_params": 3,
    "rationale": "The baseline returns an empty plan, so every goal fails. The public examples share a structure: one man starts at a location, all nuts are at one location, spanners are spread over the location graph, and spanners are consumed (useable is deleted) by tighten_nut. So a valid plan must: walk to a useable spanner, pick it up, walk to the nut location, tighten, then repeat with the next still-useable spanner. I implement BFS over directed links for walking and a greedy per-nut loop that fetches a fresh useable spanner whenever the carried one has been consumed. Goals not of form tightened(n) are best-effort; if unmet the plan is still returned (best effort within budget).",
